From a767e24047e90ee885c3ea3ec13a30ba99d8c8bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Lin <benjamin-jw.lin@mediatek.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 17:01:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: unify vendor commands for different chip
 generation

This commit squashes following commits for conciseness.

mtk: mt76: Update MAC address handling in vendor policies

Problem:
Incorrect MAC address handling in vendor attributes can lead to
improper data processing and potential errors during wireless
operations.

Root Cause:
The use of NLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN_WARN and manual MAC address extraction
led to inefficient and error-prone handling of MAC addresses.

Solution:
Replace NLA_POLICY_EXACT_LEN_WARN with NLA_POLICY_ETH_ADDR for proper
MAC address validation. Use nla_memcpy for efficient MAC address
extraction, ensuring accurate data handling.

Feature:
Stability

Signed-off-by: Peter Chiu <chui-hao.chiu@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: unify shared interface

This patch is part of a series to unify vendor commands across chip
generations.

Move the common vendor ABI to mt76 and register per-chip operations.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

