generations.

Move common TX power command validation to mt76.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: share mt7915 policies

This patch is part of a series to unify vendor commands across chip
generations.

Reuse compatible common policies in the mt7915 vendor command table.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: share mt7915 IBF control

This patch is part of a series to unify vendor commands across chip
generations.

Dispatch mt7915 IBF commands through the common vendor operations.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: share mt7915 BSS color dump

This patch is part of a series to unify vendor commands across chip
generations.

Use the common BSS color dump handler for mt7915.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: add ABI_LEGACY subcmd for distinguishing old chips

Add a new subcmd MTK_NL80211_VENDOR_SUBCMD_ABI_LEGACY to let user space
daemon be able to distinguish the chip generation, so that it can handle
the legacy vendor command paths.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: rename ABI_LEGACY to ABI_CONNAC2

For the extensibility of further ABI_CONNAC3, ABI_CONNAC5 if needed.
Add VENDOR_CMD_RAW_DATA policy to prevent kernel warning and also remove
the unnecessary attributes.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>

mtk: mt76: vendor: reuse common vendor policies for mt7915

Replace the local TX power and 3-wire vendor attribute policies with the
shared mt76 definitions.

Use the common policies both while parsing vendor attributes and when
registering the vendor commands, keeping validation consistent and
allowing mt7915 to accept the common policy extensions.

Signed-off-by: Shayne Chen <shayne.chen@mediatek.com>
